WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.475
Finally, where not to anchor.

2
00:00:02.725 --> 00:00:10.275
Not in navigation channels, cable or pipeline areas, or restricted areas, and not where you block other traffic.

3
00:00:10.525 --> 00:00:14.100
At night show your anchor light, and by day a black ball.

4
00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:17.300
That’s Rule thirty, which you already know.

5
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:23.025
In the Florida Keys National Marine Sanctuary, anchoring on coral is prohibited.

6
00:00:23.275 --> 00:00:25.900
So what do you do at a popular reef?

7
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.175
Pick up one of the mooring buoys.

8
00:00:29.425 --> 00:00:31.325
That’s what they’re there for.

9
00:00:31.575 --> 00:00:33.925
Stay off seagrass where you can.

10
00:00:34.175 --> 00:00:38.675
And leave room for the other boats to swing when the wind or tide turns.

11
00:00:38.925 --> 00:00:42.825
Everyone swings, but not everyone swings the same way.

12
00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:44.950
That’s lesson nine.

13
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.375
Match the anchor to the bottom.

14
00:00:47.625 --> 00:00:50.875
Scope is seven to one, measured from the bow.

15
00:00:51.125 --> 00:00:53.050
Lower it, don’t throw it.

16
00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.250
And always from the bow.

17
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.725
Next time: heavy weather, inlets and trouble.
